packages/main/src/core/process-fact-levels.ts:234:  { name: 'host_run', level: 'L2', category: 'managed-provider-execution', owner: 'handlers/host-run + core/managed-host-run', rationale: 'Submits one durable provider CLI execution whose worker, process group, finite absolute deadline, output projection, terminal and receipt outlive the observing caller. The handler mirrors finite-positive-integer timeout/deadline schema constraints and publishes the exact durable runId through progress before foreground attach so a replacement caller can recover without duplicate spawn. For a managed reviewer, the one-shot capability descriptor settles the controller on local write finish (not worker-side descriptor close), then the independent durable claim handshake bounds detached submission without waiting for provider terminal exit. Shared provider admission is mandatory even with usage accounting disabled, and release mutation failures remain observable. Ordinary output/usage remain diagnostic; formal --managedReview derives the immutable story/reviewRun/lane/provider/material tuple but executes the provider only in a sealed detached scratch at the submitted HEAD while the canonical Story worktree remains the durable audit root. Before launch the controller evaluates the four canonical read-only acceptance report projections in that signed root, injects only a bounded path-free status snapshot into the managed-only derived prompt, and seals that exact derived-prompt digest in the immutable run binding; providers must consume the snapshot rather than invoke those readers from scratch, and unavailable is explicit rather than a cwd-gate bypass. Only the provider adapter bounded final-result lane may produce an unimported proposal. Managed Claude alone receives its mode-0600 one-shot prompt below the exact provider cwd in a sealed runId-bound leaf; normal worker cleanup plus terminal reconciliation/expiry repair remove only that exact leaf after a crash, alongside an explicit non