packages/main/src/core/process-fact-levels.ts:239:  { name: 'managed_review_evidence_import', level: 'L4', category: 'managed-review-evidence', owner: 'handlers/managed-review-evidence + core/managed-review-evidence', rationale: 'Controller-triggerable but verdict-free importer. It accepts only runId plus exact receipt, revalidates one provider-authored proposal artifact, strict nested finding vocabulary, completed cleanup with replacementSafe/reaped/no-residual facts, live current head/material plus ReviewRun prompt/material/provider tuple, and every provider verdict/read-provenance field through shared Proof Admissibility before importing the signed ReviewPass/Finding shape. Under the exact receipt and canonical story locks, fresh managed pass and finding imports also apply the same candidate read binding as native evidence; matching candidate/corpus digests cannot substitute for the routed full reads. Receipt-id replay is serialized independently, while distinct receipts share the canonical story-level review-pass/findings locks so concurrent native and managed writers cannot lose updates or allocate duplicate ids. It writes story evidence before sealing the immutable receipt binding; a terminal-receipt-matching binding without its companion seal is recovery-only and gate-inadmissible, and idempotent replay repairs that absent seal only from exact persisted evidence. REVIEW consumption repeats the exact persisted-field checks. Registered-broker native invocation attestations, managed cross-provider receipts, advisory-only unsealed cross-provider output, and degraded-single-host local assurance remain disjoint authority classifications.', gateConsumer: 'storyMachine.canPassReview REVIEW to TEST gate through collectReviewerEvidenceState shared revalidation' },
packages/main/src/core/process-fact-levels.ts:416:  { name: 'runtime:review_execution_authority_gate', level: 'L4', category: 'runtime-behavior', owner: 'core/native-review-attestation + core/native-review-evidence + core/managed-review-evidence + core/review-run', rationale: 'REVIEW accepts direct reviewer evidence only when its ReviewPass/Finding signature seals a one-shot Ed25519 invocation attestation issued by an externally registered host-adapter broker and bound to the exact story, agent, lane, ReviewRun, writer session, signed dispatch and adapter/host identity; native finding signatures additionally bind category, evidenceState, uncertaintyReason, files, and disprovenEvidence. Lattice stores only registered broker public keys and exposes no issuer CLI or local private-key fallback. Process ancestry is optional corroboration when observable, but a visible mixed Codex/Claude ancestry is an unconditional veto. Raw provider CLI calls, missing/forged/replayed/cross-context attestations, absence of an authority binding, and degraded-single-host local facts cannot borrow native authority. Without a registered broker integration, native direct evidence is advisory-only and formal review must use the managed path. The managed cross-provider path requires one successful cleaned terminal receipt and one exact proposal created only from a schema-valid bounded Codex agent_message, exact standalone Codex raw stdout envelope, or Claude result final-result lane after successful provider exit; ordinary Codex progress agent messages are excluded, while missing, malformed, multiple, oversized, tool-log, streamed-output or controller-authored verdict input fails closed. The provider executes only in its sealed scratch while the controller-projected canonical report snapshot and its exact derived-prompt digest are sealed in the managed run binding; REVIEW verifies that sealed digest rather than granting a scratch cwd exception or re-rendering mutable report state. Exact verdict